Subject: [PATCH 10/10] Common/GPU: let a build switch on the OpenGL render trace

GLRenderManager already carries a complete trace of the handshake between the
emu thread and the render thread. Every VLOG in the file names one side of it:
which frame was begun, which task was pushed, which was pulled and run, which
wait is being sat in. It is precisely the instrument this port needs, and it was
already written.

It is behind `#if 0 // def _DEBUG`, which no build can turn on. A round that
needs the trace has to edit the file, and an instrument that has to be
hand-edited into place is one nobody reaches for.

Adding `defined(PPSSPP_GL_TRACE)` to that condition costs nothing when the
define is absent — which is every build that does not ask for it — and makes the
trace a compile flag. `make wasm GLTRACE=1` passes it here.

The `0 // def _DEBUG` half is left exactly as upstream wrote it rather than
tidied away: whatever the reason it is disabled in debug builds, it is not this
patch's business.

diff --git a/Common/GPU/OpenGL/GLRenderManager.cpp b/Common/GPU/OpenGL/GLRenderManager.cpp
index c1f03084d..ccf6f9052 100644
--- a/Common/GPU/OpenGL/GLRenderManager.cpp
+++ b/Common/GPU/OpenGL/GLRenderManager.cpp
@@ -11,7 +11,15 @@
 #include "Common/StringUtils.h"
 #include "Common/Math/math_util.h"
 
-#if 0 // def _DEBUG
+// The push/pull trace. Every VLOG in this file names one side of the handshake between
+// the emu thread and the render thread — which frame was begun, which task was pushed,
+// which was pulled and run, which wait is being sat in. It is exactly the instrument
+// needed when one of the two sides goes quiet, and it was already written; it was simply
+// switched off, and `#if 0` cannot be switched on from a build.
+//
+// Behaviour is unchanged when the define is absent, which is every build that does not
+// ask for it.
+#if defined(PPSSPP_GL_TRACE) || 0 // def _DEBUG
 #define VLOG(...) INFO_LOG(Log::G3D, __VA_ARGS__)
 #else
 #define VLOG(...)
diff --git a/Common/CMakeLists.txt b/Common/CMakeLists.txt
index 7c146831c..5b3803a17 100644
--- a/Common/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/Common/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -403,3 +403,12 @@ endif()
 # was only linked to the old combined "core" target, which happened to always be linked after
 # Common everywhere it mattered).
 target_link_libraries(Common ${GlslangLibs})
+
+# The OpenGL push/pull trace, off unless a round asks for it. Scoped to the one file
+# that has the VLOGs rather than set globally, so switching it on invalidates a single
+# object rather than the whole ccache — an instrument nobody can afford to turn on is
+# an instrument nobody turns on.
+if(PPSSPP_GL_TRACE)
+	set_source_files_properties(GPU/OpenGL/GLRenderManager.cpp PROPERTIES COMPILE_DEFINITIONS PPSSPP_GL_TRACE)
+	message(STATUS "OpenGL render trace enabled (PPSSPP_GL_TRACE)")
+endif()
